{
  "id": "ss.char.dot",
  "name": "Dot",
  "description": "A survivor sealed in an exploration suit, drawn at eight heads: dark suit fabric under a slate chest shell, a hard helmet with a black visor, sealed gloves and boots, and the dead pheromone core socketed in the chest where the hive's would be lit. No skin shows anywhere, which is the point — the hive reads scent, and a body wrapped this tight gives it nothing. What makes Dot Dot is the feelers: two dead antennae rooted at the crown of the helmet and grown to twice any other survivor's, rising, arcing back over the shoulders and hanging to the waist, slate-grey and bobble-tipped, swaying with every step and sweeping, slowly, for a signal that never comes. A scout's kit otherwise: the lightest shell of the eight, a coiled lash wound on the near forearm rather than carried, a single frost stripe on the chest and a cold blue line in the visor. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
